In addition, we also note that SyQMA provides a symbolic treatment of a $d=3$ colour code non-Clifford state injection and verification scheme, reporting a postselected LER scaling of $p^2$~\cite{syqma}.
We also thank Zhenghao (William) Zhong for the invitation to Oxford as a visitor.
We acknowledge useful discussions with Austin Fowler and Zoë Holmes.
We acknowledge the use of large language models in the refinement of the methods (especially the use of ChatGPT 6 Astra in extending the human-made $d=3$ results to the $d=5$ circuits) and wording of this manuscript. The code generated was checked and tested and we take responsibility for all contents, to the best of our abilities.
