\label{fig:window}
\end{figure}

Two positions are natural for $P(\boldsymbol u,\boldsymbol z)$, the entry side or the exit side of the Clifford part, and a simulation decides it (Sec.~\ref{app:B-checks}). The main text's two-fault pattern of Eq.~\eqref{eq:v2-fixed-fault} and Fig.~\ref{fig:d3-fault-expansion}, $X_3$ in the fold and $Y_9$ in the unfold, has net data error $Q=X_0X_3Y_9$ before the exit layer. Inserting $Q$ at the exit side reproduces the actual pattern exactly, $A=B=1/4$. Inserting it at the entry side does not: its $Z_9$ part would propagate onto ancilla 8 and fire a detector. 
Figure~\ref{fig:qposition} draws the three cases.

