\[ M=\MCzs,\quad b'=\bpCzs, \qquad \augCzs\ \longrightarrow\ \rrefCzs, \]
\conszs, no solution, $A=0$. The three ones in $b'$ are the $X$-check syndrome of $Z_7$: rejection by a syndrome shows up as inconsistency, not as an early exit. The coherent-sum computation agrees, its $2\times2$ matrix is $\bmatzs$ and the result $\binstzs$.
