\[ k=1,\ e_{\rm bit}=0,\ \ell=\boldsymbol0,\qquad M=\MCxl,\quad b'=\bpCxl \]
for $s=+1$, eight solutions, $A=\resAxl$, $B=\resBxl$. For $s=-1$ the flag flips, $b'=(0,0,0,1)$, again eight solutions, $A=\resAxlminus$, $B=\resBxlminus$. Physically $X_L\ket{T_L^\dagger}\propto\ket{T_L}$ is an equal superposition of the $M_L=\pm1$ states: half the time the check projects onto the good state, half the time onto the bad one, and the central bit records which.
\end{itemize}

